---
/**
 * The plate on the front page: an exploded view from a service manual.
 *
 * The drawing is the architecture as hardware. The chassis and the panel are
 * the markup, which stands there regardless. The bezel on top is the theme,
 * which gives the face its colours and lifts off without the panel noticing.
 * The card that pulls out of its
 * slot and goes back in is the web component. The cables bring the page in
 * from the server, and the screws are the web standards, which fit every
 * framework. The caption says which letter is which, so the drawing
 * itself is decoration and has an empty `alt`.
 *
 * The file is black ink on a transparent ground, so the paper's grain shows
 * between the lines without a blend mode. A blend mode would not have
 * worked here: the sheet is a size container, which makes it its own
 * stacking context, and the drawing then blended with nothing and stood in
 * a box of its own. The dark theme inverts the ink.
 */
---

<figure class="plate">
  <img
    class="plate__drawing"
    src="/exploded-view.webp"
    alt=""
    width="1360"
    height="1436"
    decoding="async"
  />
  <figcaption class="plate__caption">
    <span class="profile-label">Figure 1-1 · Interface unit, exploded view</span>
    <b>A</b> is the theme, the bezel that gives the face its colours and lifts
    off without the panel under it noticing.
    <b>C</b> is the chassis and <b>B</b> the panel: the markup, which stands
    there whatever happens. <b>D</b> is the web component, a card that pulls
    out and goes back without the rest noticing. <b>E</b> brings the page in
    from the server. <b>F</b> are the screws: the web standards, a thread that
    fits every frame.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .plate {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--lt-spacing-3);
  }

  .plate__drawing {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    max-inline-size: 32rem;
    block-size: auto;
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :global(:root:not([data-theme="light"])) .plate__drawing {
      filter: invert(1);
      opacity: 0.6;
    }
  }

  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .plate__drawing {
    filter: invert(1);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .plate__caption {
    font-family: var(--profile-font-data);
    font-size: var(--lt-font-size-xs);
    line-height: var(--lt-line-height-default);
    color: var(--lt-color-neutral-text-subtle);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .plate__caption .profile-label {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: var(--lt-spacing-1);
  }

  .plate__caption b {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--lt-color-neutral-text-strong);
  }
</style>
